lisa-selfreview:
Pass 1 (lenient, final): approve. Checked CORE-SEC-001 (tokens returned once, stored as
sha256 hashes, never logged), CORE-SEC-002 (enrollment routes admin-only; registration takes
exactly one credential), CORE-CONC-001 (spend and rotate are CAS updates that re-check the
hash/used state, so a concurrent second use is a 401), CORE-ID-001 (label lookup + constant-
time compare), CORE-TEST-001 (TestEnrollment, TestEnrollmentRefused, the contract flow).
Deferred should-fix: the enrollment is spent before the agent and token are written; a store
failure in between leaves a spent token with no agent (the admin re-enrolls).

lisa-design:
Enrollment and AgentRefreshToken are internal store kinds (registered in serve's file store
kinds); no internal/store change. The owner's provider is the dispatcher's sign-in provider
(auth.Provider()), passed by the handler. Only an admin's deregisterAgent revokes the refresh
token: the agent's own deregistration on shutdown must not lock it out of its restart.
